('history_text',
'Christ Foundation Gospel Church (CFGC) was founded in 1969 by the late Bishop S. A. Akintobi as a Spirit-filled, Word-based Pentecostal church. From its humble beginnings in Lagos, Nigeria, the church has grown to become a nationwide ministry with branches across Nigeria and beyond.

The church is built on the bedrock of Scripture, with a strong emphasis on evangelism, discipleship, and community service. Over the decades, CFGC has been instrumental in transforming lives through the preaching of the Gospel and practical Christian service.

