('vision_text',
'To raise a generation of Spirit-filled, Word-grounded believers who will demonstrate the Kingdom of God in every sphere of life — in their homes, communities, workplaces, and nations.'),

('mission_text',
'To preach Christ as the Sure Foundation for victorious Christian living, making disciples of all nations through evangelism, discipleship, worship, fellowship, and service.'),

('motto_text',
'Christ, the Sure Foundation — 1 Corinthians 3:11'),

('doctrines_text',
'**The Holy Scripture**
We believe the Bible is the inspired and infallible Word of God, the supreme authority in all matters of faith and conduct.

**The Trinity**
We believe in one God, eternally existing in three persons: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.

**Salvation**
We believe that all have sinned and that salvation is by grace through faith in Jesus Christ alone, through repentance and confession.

**The Holy Spirit**
We believe in the baptism of the Holy Spirit with the evidence of speaking in tongues, as the promise of the Father for empowerment for service.

**Water Baptism**
We believe in water baptism by immersion as an outward declaration of faith in Christ.

**The Church**
We believe in the universal Church, the Body of Christ, of which all true believers are members, and in the importance of regular fellowship.

**The Second Coming of Christ**
We believe in the personal, visible, and imminent return of the Lord Jesus Christ to reign in glory.'),

('youth_ministry_text',
'The CFGC Youth Ministry is dedicated to raising a generation of young people who are rooted in God''s Word, empowered by the Holy Spirit, and equipped to make a difference in their world. We provide a dynamic, fun, and faith-filled environment where young people can encounter God, build meaningful friendships, and discover their purpose.

Through weekly fellowships, Bible studies, prayer meetings, and outreach activities, our youth are challenged to grow in their relationship with God and to be salt and light in their communities. We believe that young people are not just the church of tomorrow — they are the church of today.')

